{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement (`y ~ normal(mu, sigma)`) before any other use. Both parameters have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before subsequent model-block use (`tau ~ gamma(...)`, then `mu ~ normal(...)`).
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  vector[N] y;
  real mu0;
  real<lower=0> lambda0;
  real<lower=0> alpha0;
  real<lower=0> beta0;
}
parameters {
  real mu;
  real<lower=0> tau;
}
transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma = inv_sqrt(tau);
}
model {
  tau ~ gamma(alpha0, beta0);
  mu ~ normal(mu0, inv_sqrt(lambda0 * tau));
  y ~ normal(mu, sigma);
}
generated quantities {
  real y_rep = normal_rng(mu, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":10,"y":[-0.3,0.1,0.4,0.2,-0.1,0.6,0.0,0.3,0.5,0.2],"mu0":0.0,"lambda0":1.0,"alpha0":2.0,"beta0":2.0}","protected_variables":["y"]}
